0	section	Talking to Sithik Ints in ogre form
1	line	Sithik Ints	Arghhhh..what's happened to me...you beast!
1	line	Player	It's your own fault, you shouldn't have lied about your involvement with the undead Ogres at Jiggig. The potion will wear off once you've told the truth!
1	line	Sithik Ints	Ok, ok, I admit it, I got Brentle Vahn to cast the spell to put an end to those awful Ogres...they're just disgusting creatures...
1	line	Player	Ok, that's a start...now I want some answers.
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	How do I remove the effects of the spell from the area?
2	line	Player	How do I remove the effects of the spell from the area? The ogres want to get their ceremonial dance area back and can't do that with undead walking all over it.
2	cond	Asking for the first time:
3	line	Sithik Ints	Unfortunately you can't. The spell is permanent, it will last forever, the only option you have is to move the ceremonial area.
3	line	Player	You're an evil man and I'm going to make you pay for this...you can stay like that forever as far as I'm concerned.
3	line	Sithik Ints	No...no, let me try to make amends...please I can help you. Just don't leave me like this.
3	action	previous
2	cond	Asking him again:
3	line	Sithik Ints	Haven't I told you this already? You can't remove the spell, it's permanent, it will last forever, the only option you have is to move the ceremonial area.
3	line	Player	You're an evil man and I'm going to make you pay for this...you can stay like that forever as far as I'm concerned.
3	line	Sithik Ints	No...no, let me try to make amends...please I can help you. Just don't leave me like this.
3	action	previous
1	option	How do I get rid of the undead ogres?
2	line	Player	How do I get rid of the undead ogres?
2	cond	Asking for the first time:
3	line	Sithik Ints	Ok, similar spells have been cast before and the only way to deal with the resulting creatures is to cordon off the area and not go in there again.
3	line	Sithik Ints	The undead creatures usually manifest some sort of disease so it's best to attack them from a distance with a ranged weapon.
3	line	Sithik Ints	Normal missiles like arrows and darts do very little damage to them because they're designed to destroy internal organs. This is a waste of time with undead creatures like undead ogres.
3	line	Player	Yeah, clearly so what should we use?
3	line	Sithik Ints	From my research it looks like a flat ended arrow was designed called a 'Brutal arrow'. This does large amounts of crushing damage to the creature. You can make them by using larger arrows.
3	line	Sithik Ints	I think some Ogre hunters make them. But instead of adding an arrow tip, you hammer a large nail into the end of the shaft.
3	action	previous
2	cond	Asking him again:
3	line	Sithik Ints	Haven't I already explained this to you once before?
3	line	Player	Humour me!
3	action	(Continues with "Ok, similar spells...")
1	option	How do I get rid of the disease?
2	line	Player	How do I get rid of the disease?
2	cond	Asking for the first time:
3	line	Sithik Ints	My research shows that two jungle based herbs can be used, one is found near river tributaries and looks like a vine, the other is found in caves and grows on the wall.
3	line	Sithik Ints	It's quite well camouflaged so it's unlikely that you'll find it.
3	line	Player	We'll see about that!
3	action	previous
2	cond	Asking him again as an ogre:
3	line	Sithik Ints	Haven't I already explained this disease thing to you once before?
3	line	Player	Just tell me again or else I'll never turn you back into a human!
3	line	Sithik Ints	No...noo...please, I'll tell you.
3	action	(Continues with "My research shows...")
2	cond	Asking him again as a human:
3	line	Sithik Ints	Haven't I already explained this disease thing to you once before?
3	line	Player	Just tell me again or I'll turn you back into an ogre.
3	line	Sithik Ints	No...noo...please, I'll tell you.
3	action	(Continues with "My research shows...")
1	option	Sorry, I have to go.
2	line	Player	Sorry, I have to go.
2	line	Sithik Ints	But...you can't just leave me here like this!
2	action	end
